Iteration 1 complete. Here's what I accomplished toward the **Parallel Stage Execution Engine with Dependency Graph Scheduler** goal:

## Summary

I built the **foundational pure DAG library** — the core of the whole feature, and the piece everything else depends on (Tasks 1–4 of the plan).

**Created `scripts/lib/pipeline-dag.sh`** — a side-effect-free, jq-only library (bash 3.2 compatible, no associative arrays):
- `dag_default_depends_on` — injects a linear `depends_on` chain for enabled stages lacking one. This is the guarantee of **byte-identical sequential behaviour** when no template opts in (backward compat). It correctly preserves explicit deps (including explicit `[]` roots) and never touches disabled stages.
- `dag_validate_acyclic` — Kahn's-algorithm cycle detection + missing/disabled-dep rejection, reporting `E_DAG_CYCLE` / `E_DAG_MISSING_DEP` with the offending path to stderr.
- `dag_compute_layers` — topological layering with stable within-layer order for determinism (diamond `A→{B,C}→D` ⇒ `A | B C | D`).
- A CLI entrypoint (`layers|validate|defaults`) for debugging.

**Created `scripts/sw-pipeline-dag-test.sh`** — 28 unit tests, all passing:
- **Test pyramid (this layer):** 28 unit tests covering the scheduler's pure business logic. Integration/E2E (`run_pipeline` flag parity, wall-clock benchmark) come in later iterations once the executor exists.
- **Critical paths covered:** happy path (diamond, wide fan-out, single stage); error cases (2-cycle, transitive 3-cycle, missing dep, dep-on-disabled); edge cases (linear-default sequential parity, explicit-`[]` root, disabled-stage exclusion, determinism across 5 runs).

Registered the suite in `package.json` and verified bash-3.2 compatibility + syntax. Both commits are in.

## Remaining work (not complete — not declaring LOOP_COMPLETE)
Tasks 5–14 still pending: `pipeline-parallel.sh` (partition + run-layer + log merge), `run_pipeline()` integration behind `SW_PARALLEL_STAGES`, composer wiring, template `depends_on`, docs, and the >30% wall-clock benchmark. Next iteration will build `pipeline-parallel.sh`.
